const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文讨论利用财务报表变量组织对盈余操纵风险的分析框架。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"The paper discusses a framework for analyzing earnings-manipulation risk with financial-statement variables. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2469/faj.v55.n5.2296",label:{zh:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"公开说明以多个财务指标的组合和历史比较为基础，而不是以单一比率作决定性判别。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"Its public description combines several financial indicators and historical comparisons instead of making one ratio dispositive. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2469/faj.v55.n5.2296",label:{zh:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"输入包括经版本控制的财务报表、会计科目定义、公司行动、报告期和实际披露日期。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"Inputs are versioned financial statements, accounting definitions, corporate actions, reporting periods, and actual disclosure dates. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2469/faj.v55.n5.2296",label:{zh:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"研究提供风险筛查与解释框架，不能把任何分数或比率直接视为操纵事实或法律结论。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"It is a screening and interpretation framework; no score or ratio is itself a fact of manipulation or a legal conclusion. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not convert association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2469/faj.v55.n5.2296",label:{zh:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"保留单位、币种、合并范围和重述，按当时可得信息构造指标，并记录缺失值与行业口径处理。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Retain units, currency, consolidation scope, and restatements; construct variables as-of date; record missing-value and industry treatment. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2469/faj.v55.n5.2296",label:{zh:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Financial Analysts Journal (1999)。会计模型的历史样本和定义并不替代审计证据；该导读不作公司评价、执法判断或投资建议。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Financial Analysts Journal (1999). A historical accounting model does not replace audit evidence and this guide makes no company, enforcement, or investment judgment. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2469/faj.v55.n5.2296",label:{zh:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Financial Analysts Journal (1999) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Detection of Earnings Manipulation”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。会计模型的历史样本和定义并不替代审计证据；该导读不作公司评价、执法判断或投资建议。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Detection of Earnings Manipulation”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
